KNOWNBUG gcc-only
main.cpp
--cpp11
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ returned or thrown: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ length_error thrown: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.3\] line \d+ WRONG \(must FAIL\): FAILURE$
^\*\* 1 of \d+ failed
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
^CONVERSION ERROR$
--
CBMC took a call of the body-less helpers to return, so allocate() with
n > 4 fell off its end and returned an arbitrary pointer.  With GCC 16.2's
headers this made cpp11_ostream_integer_formatting run past 900 s
(24 s now).
